{
  "based_on_commit": "27455801694a5e8d1338335f93d4e66d8410fc24",
  "based_on_tag": "v0.5.0",
  "changes": [
    "Independent v6 package and launchers; legacy, v4 and v5 frozen.",
    "Bundled validated 1850--2036 planet reference with separate interpolated proposal and exact authority interfaces.",
    "Batched exact visit refinement, deterministic per-planet workers, structured telemetry, and a controlled v5/v6 benchmark.",
    "Conservative two-anchor constellation recruitment tests all compatible one-to-one overrides and can recover a third or later Gaia-associated planet after a common-epoch refit, with explicit JSON/CSV audit fields.",
    "Closed centred full-horizon footprints provide a provisional image-centre zenith when extinction is not identifiable; boundary circle residuals, complete azimuth coverage and fitted-camera 90-degree rays reject ellipses, crops and round vignettes; strong photometric solutions retain authority and the rejected trial remains auditable.",
    "Accepted stellar fields activate nighttime solar consistency; global fixed-sample stellar-horizon zenith bounds reject daylight planet aliases while preserving twilight refits, unresolved geometry, alternative identities and complete audit records.",
    "Native-depth PNG/TIFF and mono/RGB/RG1G2B FITS ingestion preserves scientific samples, records scaling/channel/saturation provenance, masks invalid pixels, retains both green planes, and confines uint8 stretching to display products.",
    "Post-release automatic append-only SQLite recording for every go6 analysis, including reruns and partial failures; all textual scientific evidence and CSV measurements retained without quality cuts, deduplication, or feedback into blind fitting.",
    "Post-release audited recognition-only Gaussian fallback for undersampled FITS point sources; native samples retain peak and flux authority.",
    "Post-release unresolved status for exhausted proper-motion reassociation, retaining the last internally consistent fitted camera and membership."
  ],
